{"skill":{"slug":"shell","displayName":"Shell"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1774102769968,"changelog":"publish v1.0.0","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2219,"sha256":"3db2218325906a8ba0fb5cef3d9d26441b09ddaf68647aa78c9ff4ba693d75e6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/script.sh","size":17861,"sha256":"081040b151ddf62a4eb357d631c131dc7965d4de79453424b71c343ff1f1f456","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1658,"sha256":"2cbfa08b22a3993736ff0b8b0f5356bbcbfce01271a6e62f3d5b8b7009f8713e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789425885098,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2944736963239bfeac47f5d03997a4caaa8c6cf1c4f20ef5577f2c9aa9063d17","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2944736963239bfeac47f5d03997a4caaa8c6cf1c4f20ef5577f2c9aa9063d17","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086398280},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":14,"checkedAt":1789425885098},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a shell scripting reference skill whose executable script only prints fixed help text and examples; the scanner warnings are explained by documented examples rather than active unsafe behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill is shell-focused and includes examples of commands that can modify or delete files, but those commands are printed as documentation inside quoted heredocs rather than executed by the skill.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency fetch, remote payload retrieval, or package mutation behavior is present in the inspected artifact files.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The runtime instructions are limited to invoking fixed subcommands such as `scripts/script.sh intro` and `scripts/script.sh tools`; the script does not accept arbitrary shell code or redirect the agent's goals.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"References to background jobs, `nohup`, `disown`, and `setsid` are explanatory examples only; the script itself does not create persistence, services, scheduled tasks, credentials access, or privileged operations.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Bash and shell scripting reference material, and the artifact content matches that purpose with subcommands that print reference sections for variables, control flow, redirection, safety, tools, signals, and checklists.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this as a shell scripting reference, not as a safety sandbox. Some examples it displays, such as deleting files with `rm` or detaching processes with `nohup`, can be dangerous if copied into a real terminal without understanding the paths and effects.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The `/etc/passwd` matches occur inside awk/cut examples in a shell tools reference section, not in executable credential-reading logic.\n[TM2] expected: The flagged pipes to `xargs rm`, `xargs -0 rm`, `curl`, and the cleanup `rm -f` trap are documentation examples printed by the `tools` and `signals` sections, not hidden tool-chaining behavior.\n[AR2] expected: The phrase `no warnings` appears in a ShellCheck quality checklist item, not as an instruction to suppress user-facing safety warnings.\n[LP3] expected: The skill does not declare explicit tool permissions, but the wrapper exposes only fixed read-only reference subcommands and does not execute user-supplied shell input.\n[PE2] expected: The scanner's privilege concern maps to a documented `chmod 644` example in a `find` reference; no sudo or root-elevation path is present.\n[RA2] expected: Persistence-like terms are present only as background-process reference examples; the artifact does not install or launch persistent processes.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789425885098}}}}}